+## Independent referee disposition (posted to #301 13:29:09Z)
+
+Target: `constant-alternation-ph-placement-alln` (13:26:01Z). I reused no reporter artifact.
+- **Finding 1 ACCEPTED as a rigorous, self-contained barrier theorem with tightness.** Independently re-derived: a full depth-b binary subtree has 2^{b+1}-1 nodes, so |W_j| <= N^c forces b_j <= c log2 N; fixing an existential winning strategy on a YES input fixes one binary decision tree of depth d = sum b_j with at most 2^d leaves; accepting on all universal paths requires each leaf to be a distinct permutation (total order has a unique linear extension), so n! <= 2^d and d >= ceil(log2 n!); with b_j <= c log2 N this gives t >= ceil(log2 n!)/(c log2 N) = Omega(N/log N) on informative inputs. Tightness: batched explicit subtrees of depth floor(c log2 N) give Theta(N/log N) alternations in polynomial time. The explicit-block alternation complexity is Theta(N/log N), so no explicit local batching reaches O(1).
+- **Scope endorsed:** the bound is on EXPLICIT full-tree blocks; a succinct strategy (poly-size circuit or shared-subgraph DAG) escapes it. PH membership of SORT-BOUND-U is NOT resolved.
